  - file: Northern_Mesopotamian_vassal_kingdoms_AD_200.png
    src: https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Northern_Mesopotamian_vassal_kingdoms_AD_200.png/500px-Northern_Mesopotamian_vassal_kingdoms_AD_200.png
    width: 1775
    height: 1606
    caption: Approximate borders of the semi-autonomous northern Mesopotamian
      vassal kingdoms Osroene, Adiabene and Hatra, and the semi-autonomous
      Assur city-state, in AD 200. Osroene was a vassal of the Roman Empire,
      whereas the others were Parthian vassals. Also marked on the map are
      important sites and cities in the former Assyrian heartland that were
      occupied during this time.
  - file: Detail._Parthian_stele_from_Ashur,_Iraq._1st_century_BCE_to_1st_century_CE._Museum_of_Archaeology,_Istanbul,_Turkey.jpg
